    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0480" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg406"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Clay</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 191.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,
                            Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 6, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received with great satisfaction
                    your despatch No. 99, of the 6th of February, and its accompanying report of the
                    proceedings at the banquet given by the merchants of Moscow to the American
                    legation and the mayor of that city.</p>
                <p>The details of this feast have been already indirectly published, and they have
                    excited an influence favorable to the present growth of friendship towards
                    Russia, which is even now a unanimous sentiment of the American people.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cassius M. Clay</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
